      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "**banking-dev** · ECS Fargate · Singapore · CloudWatch, 60-second buckets.\n\n**Configured deployment:** 0.5 vCPU / **2 GiB (2048 MiB) per task**; app limit/reservation 1536/1024 MiB, Alloy 512/256 MiB. **Configured autoscaling:** CPU **60%**, memory **70%**, **2–4 tasks**, scale-out/in cooldown **30s / 60s**. These are deployment settings, not live control-plane metrics; check ECS for rollout revision and scaling activity.\n\nCPU/memory panels query actual **AWS/ECS service utilization**, including the sidecar. AWS defines service MemoryUtilization against reserved memory and specifies that memoryReservation affects the calculation. Configured app + Alloy reservations total **1280 MiB**; this is configuration, not measured usage. The **2048 MiB task hard limit** is separate and is not asserted as the CloudWatch denominator. JVM heap is shown separately on [Overview](/d/banking-api-overview).\n\nHealthy ALB targets and application scrapes are readiness/telemetry counts, not ECS desired/running counts. **Live ECS tasks** queries native LiveTaskCount, including ACTIVATING, RUNNING and DEACTIVATING (draining) states. It is not desired capacity or a RUNNING-only count; deployment overlap can exceed the configured 2–4 desired-task range. Desired counts, task capacity and scaling activity are not exported. Container Insights is disabled; absolute task memory usage is not corroborated, so utilization is not converted to bytes. Sparse request/error samples remain gaps; latest CloudWatch values may lag by a few minutes.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "ECS Fargate infrastructure · Singapore",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
